    <Instrument_Host>
        <name>Firefly Aerospace's Blue Ghost lunar lander</name>
        <type>Lander</type>
        <naif_host_id>-2711</naif_host_id>
        <description> 
            The Blue Ghost is a commercial lunar lander by Firefly Aerospace. It was designed to deliver payloads to the Moon 
            providing power/data for surface operations. It features a composite structure, four legs, a main engine, smaller 
            thrusters, avionics, batteries, solar power, and communication systems for long-duration missions. Standing 2 m 
            (6.6 ft) tall and 3.5 m (11.5 ft) wide, Blue Ghost was designed for stability with shock absorbing feet, a low center 
            of mass, and a wide footprint.
        </description>
